<p>Yeah, CPM trumps Bq and whatever else in this case, and it was something of a derp on my side, and the above isn't a measure I'd object to.</p>
<p>That said, power incident does have its uses as most dosimetric measurements are based on received energy from radiation - therefore all it takes is assume reasonable area for a human body, and work out how high would it have to be to deposit a dangerous dose over a reasonable time someone is expected to be in the chamber.</p>
