<p>Alright, well I'm glad we could clear that up. I'll edit the article in short order.</p>
<p>As for the anomalous elements damaging the laws of chemistry, eh, I suppose this gets into a philosophical conundrum. When people write from the POV of other GOIs, one of the main criticisms leveled at the SCP Foundation is their commitment to enforcing &quot;consensus reality.&quot; Perhaps the Foundation believes that because these elements do not conform to the established scientific model of chemistry, they are anomalous (that is kind of what the word means, after all) and thus potentially harmful. I think I'll let the readers decide for themselves on this score.</p>

