			<div class="content" id="post-content-2120899">
									

<p>First, I want to state that this is an increidbly good article for someone who has been here for barely a day, so I'll give it that to you. Sadly, it's not good enough for me to upvote bud.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Some of these anomalous elements are listed on the Foundation’s expanded periodic table, but most are not.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>Human beings exposed to this effect will begin to show symptoms similar to heavy metal poisoning, radiation sickness, and [DATA EXPUNGED].</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The first sentence bugs me for some reason. Mostly because it reminds me the usual newbie's grammar. As for the second, redacting the last (and possibly most interesting side effect of this thing) is quite boring and overused. And you've done it several times throughout the article, so I'll better give a no-vote.</p>
<p>Now, for the good side, it's a simple idea that doesn't need a super complicated story behind to work by itself, and it's rather weird to see those nowadays<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-964991-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-964991-1')">1</a></sup>.</p>
